{"id": "0469991b-f7f2-49d9-8685-6dda0009a3a0", "role": "assistant", "block_type": "thinking", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Server-side latency looks flat with no clear regression, though I can't pin down an exact migration date. Bedrock-side latency stays steady too—Nova Lite around 950ms, Sonnet 5 averaging 7–9s with spikes to 16–17s on Nov 10 and Nov 17—but these account-level metrics may not map directly to this app, and the server-side numbers exclude client network effects.

The cross-region hop from eu-west-1 to us-east-1 adds roughly 70–100ms RTT, plus TCP/TLS handshake overhead of about 3 RTT (~250ms) for new connections if keepalive isn't used, and "us." inference profiles may route across multiple US regions adding further latency. I should suggest switching to an EU inference profile and reusing connections, while being careful not to overstate which EU profiles exist—better to recommend checking via list_inference_profiles in eu-west-1 rather than asserting availability. I could just run that check myself since it's read-only and would strengthen the answer, but I'll mention it as an offer instead of acting unprompted.

